  "description": "Meta-package bundling TINS.Native.win-x64, TINS.Native.linux-x64, and TINS.Native.osx-arm64, so a multi-platform consumer (e.g. a cross-targeted test project) can pull in native OpenBLAS/PocketFFT assets for every desktop RID with a single reference instead of adding each RID package individually. A single-RID deployment should still reference just its own TINS.Native.<rid> package directly -- this carries no native content of its own. osx-x64 is deliberately excluded, see the PackageReference comment below. FFTW is not included here, per the FFTW/core license split (GPL-2.0-or-later vs. BSD-3-Clause) -- see TINS.Native.FFTW.Desktop for the equivalent opt-in bundle.",
